# Paying life is losing it (CR 119.4), so Bloodletter of Aclazotz doubles life an opponent pays on its controller's turn.
# Bot2 plays Marsh Flats on its turn 2 and cracks it on Bot1's turn 3: the cost is 1 life, and Bot2 loses 2 (20 -> 18).
# On its own turn 4 Bot2 cracks Polluted Delta for the same 1 life, and loses only 1 (18 -> 17).

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Black Lotus
Bloodletter of Aclazotz
Swamp x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Marsh Flats
Polluted Delta
Island x5
Island
Swamp x4
Island x8

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Bloodletter of Aclazotz.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Marsh Flats.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Marsh Flats.Activate
Bot2.Choose(Tap Marsh Flats)
Bot2.Choose(Pay 1 life)
? Bot2.Life = 18
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Search(Swamp)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Polluted Delta.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Polluted Delta.Activate
Bot2.Choose(Tap Polluted Delta)
Bot2.Choose(Pay 1 life)
? Bot2.Life = 17
Bot2.Pass
Bot2.Search(Swamp)

[Expect]
Turn = 4
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot2.Battlefield = Swamp; Swamp
